{title: 258 - Baptize Us Anew}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #258 • BAPTIZE US ANEW • 11.11}
{lyricist: W. A. Ogden}
{composer: W. A. Ogden}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 258}
{meta: tune BAPTIZE US ANEW}
{meta: meter 11.11}
{meta: category Holy Spirit - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Baptize [D7]us anew [G]With power from on [C]high,
[C]With love, O refresh us! Dear [G]Savior, draw [D]nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]We humbly beseech [D]Thee, Lord Jesus, [G/D]we [D]pray,
[G]With love [C]and the Spirit baptize us today.
[G]We praise Thee, we bless Thee, dear Lamb that was slain
[C]We laud and adore [G/D]Thee, Amen [D7]and Amen.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Unworthy we cry, Unholy, unclean,
[C]O wash us and cleanse us From [G]sin's guilty [D]stain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]O heavenly Dove, Descend from on [C]high!
[C]We plead Thy rich blessing; In [G]mercy draw [D]nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]O list [D7]the [G]glad voice! From heaven it [C]came:
[C]Thou art My beloved, Well [G]pleased I [D]am.
{end_of_verse}
